--- Note ---
Both Method A and Method B returned a literal "Execution error" instead
of a real reply here — the same nested-Claude-Code-session artifact
documented in case-01-solar-pro4.log: this local verification run itself
executes from inside a Claude Code Desktop session, and the spawned
`claude` subprocess inherits that host session's own CLAUDE_CODE_*/
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL environment, which conflicts with the env vars this
script exports for its own child `claude` calls. This is specific to
running Case 01's raw-CLI methods (A/B/C/D) *from inside a nested Claude
Code session* — it does not occur in GitHub Actions CI (a clean runner
environment with no ambient Claude Code session), where Case 01 has
extensive, already-documented passing evidence (see README.md's Method
A/B/C/D transcripts and evidence-run links) confirmed via a normal CI
run, and does not occur via the Claude Agent SDK's isolated subprocess
env (see case-03-solar-open2.log below). Solar Open 2's own support in
Case 01 is not in question here — CI evidence already establishes it;
this note documents why a *local* re-run from this particular dev
environment doesn't add new signal beyond what CI already shows.
